<article class="env-lemma" id="02JU">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02JU">Lemma <span data-tag="02JU">29.53.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Let $x \in X$, and set $s = f(x)$. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$S$ is locally Noetherian, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$f$ is locally of finite type, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$X$ and $S$ integral, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$f$ dominant. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> We have </p>
  <div class="equation" id="02JV">
    <span class="equation-label"><a href="/tag/02JV" data-tag="02JV">29.53.1.1</a></span>
  <div>\begin{equation}  \label{morphisms-equation-dimension-formula} \dim (\mathcal{O}_{X, x}) \leq \dim (\mathcal{O}_{S, s}) + \text{trdeg}_{R(S)}R(X) - \text{trdeg}_{\kappa (s)} \kappa (x). \end{equation}</div>
</div>
  <p> Moreover, equality holds if $S$ is universally catenary. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The corresponding algebra statement is Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/02IJ" data-tag="02IJ">10.113.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>